    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d898">

                <pb facs="1024" n="1012" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg1012"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811B.142/4: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-11">January 11,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received January 11—10:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>225. American interests—Far East. Contents Department’s 2885 December 22<anchor
                        n="96" xml:id="d898-f1"/> transmitted Swiss Legation Tokyo.</p>
                <p>Swiss Foreign Office reports January 9 following: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Swiss Minister Tokyo states despite several personal endeavors [he has]
                            not succeeded up to present obtain reply from Japanese Government this
                            subject, difficulties apparently caused by unwillingness agree <pb
                                facs="1025" n="1013" xml:id="pg1013"/> direct remittance funds to
                            American citizens or distribution relief through Swiss
                            representative.</p>
                        <p>Minister Gorgé therefore proposed Japanese Government accept designation
                            delegate Intercroixrouge<anchor n="97" xml:id="d898-f2"/> to distribute
                            $25,000 to American citizens Manila as already done Hong Kong.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d898-f1" n="96" xml:id="d898-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed (811B.142/2 Suppl.); it stated that immediate financial assistance to
                    Americans in the Philippines was urgently required and asked for the Swiss
                    Government’s suggestion as to practical means of making American funds available
                    to these Americans should the Japanese Government not be favorably disposed to
                    the Department’s proposal. This proposal, set forth in telegram No. 2075,
                    September 1, 1942, to the Minister in Switzerland (811B.142/1a), entailed
                    sending $25,000 of American Red Cross funds to its Philippine Chapter.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d898-f2" n="97" xml:id="d898-f2-content">
                <p>International Red Cross Committee at Geneva, or Intercross.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
